  "label": "Round 5 (historical Trial 7) plus conditional continuation to six counted trials",
  "limitations": [
    "Round 5 (historical Trial 7) launched five fresh concurrent attempts, one per package, same providers as Round 4. The continuation then conditionally launched further single attempts per task -- only after that task's most recent counted result was reward-zero -- up to six counted trials with three Codex and three Claude, stopping any task immediately on a reward-one result.",
    "Route policy stopped after Round 5's pass (historicalTrial 7): 5 scored, 3 failures, 2 Codex + 3 Claude, 1 authorized slot deliberately unused. This is the user's explicit stop-on-pass rule, not a resource limit or a claim the task cannot reach a higher count.",
    "Browser replay uses coverage-v3 starting this round (adds a permitted existing-dialog recovery case coverage-v2 omitted). Its own Round 4/historical-Trial-6 Codex attempt is excluded from counting (original reward 1, diagnostic regrade 0, counted reward null); this round's four fresh attempts (T7-T10) are new, separately-counted results that fill that void and also resolve the package's previously-missing counted Claude slot (left by an earlier, still-separately-unscored Round 3/Trial 5 Claude infrastructure interruption).",
    "The __proto__ opaque-token shape-gate bug (checkers building a plain object as a token-keyed dictionary, which cannot represent the literal key \"__proto__\" as an own property) recurred in the large majority of this round's Claude attempts and in one of browser replay's Claude attempts, while Codex attempts more often produced genuine (if imperfect) per-candidate scoring. This is an observed pattern across this round, not a proven general provider tendency.",
    "Raw captures and submissions remain private; this publication retains allowlisted fields and artifact hashes."
  ],
